Z||000007||Carrolles||05-17-99||05:14 PM||||I'd love to have an 88GT but for now I'll have to do with my 85SE 2m6 4spd with the ws6 suspension.<br>From what I've heard the most bang for the buck on non-88GT cars for performance improvement is to install a rear anti-sway bar.  The 88GT has one already.<br>If you are short on funds this is the most important improvement.  Modifying the suspension to remove bump steer is an expensive proposition.  A rear sway bar does more good in the long run because it keeps the largest contact patch between the tires and the road surface.<br>A friend in Huntsville Alabama has installed Sunbird front sway bars on the rear of three of his cars ($5.00 each at the junk yard) with quite impressive results.
Z||000008||theogre||05-17-99||07:36 PM||||Carrolle you nasty tease.<p>tell us what additional parts he used and where he got them. I can't think of anyone who is to cheap to do that one. tho I can think of a few who are to lazy,,,,  :)<p>I like my 87SC, but a rear sway would be nice. especially a cheap one. Heck, we all could go harvesting, and make a package out of it that we could sell for a few bucks.
